# SECTION 3: what the pair shows

The PRE run records export_file None and its run directory holds no gen_export.txt, so a checker fire in that
run would leave nothing per-record behind. The POST run writes the stream and records export_origin 'default',
so the name came from the feature-group rule and not from an entry or an operator. The verdict is PASS on both,
which is the property worth checking: export_check FAILs a PASS run that names an export file and writes none or
writes one without a header, so a default turned on carelessly could have turned passing runs into failures.

Both plusarg lists above are quoted from the runs' own run_cmd.sh, so the difference between the two argvs is
visible rather than described.

